<%# /u/:username — the public user page (Studio::PublicUsersController).

    AVATAR AND USERNAME, NOTHING ELSE (operator's call, 2026-09-30). No name,
    email or wallet, and the image alt is the username for the same reason:
    _avatar's default alt is display_name, which a host may build from a name.

    The preview is the avatar when one is attached; `link_preview image:` treats
    an empty attachment as a blank rung, so an account with no picture unfurls
    with the site identity's image. The avatar URL is the primitive's permanent
    one (public service URL or the storage proxy), never a signed expiring URL.
    The description is left to the site identity. %>
<% username = @public_user.username.to_s %>
<% content_for(:title, username) %>
<% link_preview image: @public_user.avatar, title: username %>

<div class="max-w-md mx-auto px-4 py-12" data-public-user="<%= username %>">
  <div class="card p-8 flex flex-col items-center text-center gap-4">
    <% if @public_user.avatar.attached? %>
      <%= render "components/avatar", user: @public_user, size: "xl", alt: username %>
    <% else %>
      <%# Drawn from the username alone: a host's avatar_initials / avatar_color may read the name or email (cyvasse's do). %>
      <% colors = Studio::AVATAR_COLORS %>
      <div class="w-28 h-28 text-4xl rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-white"
           style="background-color: <%= colors[Digest::MD5.hexdigest(username).hex % colors.size] %>"><%= username[0].upcase %></div>
    <% end %>
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-heading break-all" data-public-user-username><%= username %></h1>
  </div>
</div>
